WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.920
- So you know Elton John pretty well?

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.870
- Well, so Elton's husband David and I

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.090
went to high school together.
- Random.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.542
- 400 years ago in Toronto.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.360
And we've stayed friends,
and so we got to,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.902
I mean it was a crazy time
when we first reconnected,

00:00:15.902 --> 00:00:17.824
as Will and Grace was just starting.

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:19.650
I actually said to my wife,

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.260
I think Elton and David
are coming over for dinner.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.120
- Did she freak out?

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.357
- She freaked out, I freaked out.

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:29.280
But logic sat in and we barbecued.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.670
- Okay, I was gonna say what
do you serve Sir Elton John?

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.120
- Pretty much anything.
- Okay.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.440
- He's not picky.
- Okay.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.420
- But--
- I can roll with that.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.300
All right.
- But I always tell this story

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.280
'cause we had a new piano at the time

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.010
and I was just learning to play.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.710
And it's the four of us and my son,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.840
who is six months old,
and I got up the nerve.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.370
I said, Elton, you know you
have to christen the piano?

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.960
- Elton John christened your piano?

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.889
- Yeah, so he goes in the,
(audience applauding)

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:56.200
he goes into the other room,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.710
just down the street, and
he goes and he sits down

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:03.200
and he says, "What would
you like me to play?"

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.490
and I'm so in this moment
I so want him to know me

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.620
and know that I am a big fan.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.430
So I'm not gonna say Rocket Man.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:10.514
- No, that would be obvious.

00:01:10.514 --> 00:01:12.133
- Right, so obviously I said,

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.130
I've seen that movie, too,

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.890
from Goodbye Yellow Brick Road.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.097
And he looked up at me and says,

00:01:19.097 --> 00:01:21.146
"Oh bugger off, I don't
remember that song."

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:22.290
(audience laughing)

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.390
- You were trying to be cool

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.735
and he was like, pick the hit, boy!

00:01:25.735 --> 00:01:26.774
(audience laughing)

